WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:10.866
Targets currently having lunch.

2
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:14.833
My, my, don’t they look happy.

3
00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:18.200
- Not after we catch all of them!
- Wobbuffet!

4
00:00:18.266 --> 00:00:20.133
On their way to Cyllage City,

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.900
our heroes are taking an enjoyable lunch break.

6
00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:26.866
But, little do they know mysterious eyes are watching them.

7
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.866
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

8
00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:35.433
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.166
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

10
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:41.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

11
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.300
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

12
00:00:44.366 --> 00:00:47.033
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

13
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

14
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

15
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:55.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

16
00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:58.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

17
00:01:08.066 --> 00:01:10.000
-Pi? Pika?

18
00:01:10.066 --> 00:01:13.500
- Huh?
- Ches! Ches! Chespin!

19
00:01:13.566 --> 00:01:17.500
What’s wrong?

20
00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:22.733
- It sounds like something's moving.
- Hope it’s a Pokémon!

21
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.466
Froakie!

22
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:29.466
- There is something over there!
- Pikachu!

23
00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:34.933
- Cham, Cham, Cham!
- Huh?

24
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.033
- What are they?
- Never seen those Pokémon before.

25
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.933
Wobbuffet!

26
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.166
I believe they’re Pancham.

27
00:01:44.266 --> 00:01:46.433
Sorry to scare you like that.

28
00:01:50.766 --> 00:01:55.000
Pancham, the Playful Pokémon. Though it tries to look tough,

29
00:01:55.066 --> 00:01:58.399
Pancham has trouble being taken seriously by opponents.

30
00:01:58.466 --> 00:01:59.933
Okay, that should do it.

31
00:02:00.066 --> 00:02:02.800
But those Pancham look so different.

32
00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:08.299
- Cham, Cham, Cham!
- These two are much cuter!

33
00:02:08.366 --> 00:02:11.433
The Pokédex says they do their best to look tough.

34
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.033
So I guess this must be their normal face.

35
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.533
So then they should make them cuter in the Pokédex pic!

36
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.966
I’ve never heard anyone complain about their Pokédex before.

37
00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:24.700
Really? It’s just too bad they’re being shown like that.

38
00:02:26.466 --> 00:02:29.500
- Ches? Pin?
- Cham, Cham!

39
00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.299
- Pika! Pika!
- Fennekin?

40
00:02:31.366 --> 00:02:33.299
Ches?

41
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:36.299
- Pan Cham, Cham!
- Pan Cham!

42
00:02:36.366 --> 00:02:38.500
I wonder what those two are saying.

43
00:02:38.566 --> 00:02:41.799
Maybe they’re asking if Chespin will share its Pokémon food.

44
00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:45.299
Maybe not. I wish we knew what they meant!

45
00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:51.299
Hm. Leave that to me! The future is now, thanks to science!

46
00:02:51.366 --> 00:02:53.299
Clemontic Gear on!

47
00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:57.299
Allow me to present my Pokémon Translator!

48
00:02:57.366 --> 00:03:00.200
- Wow!
- You’ve got to get better at names.

49
00:03:00.266 --> 00:03:02.366
But it sounds fascinating, for sure!

50
00:03:02.433 --> 00:03:06.100
My brilliant invention allows the user to understand Pokémon,

51
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:08.866
which facilitates better communication with Pokémon

52
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:13.333
by performing a complete analysis of vocal tone, movement and expression!

53
00:03:13.399 --> 00:03:17.399
Pancham, would you please say something? Switch on!

54
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.600
- Pan Cham, Cham!
- Pan Cham, Cham!

55
00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:23.100
What you have belongs to everyone.

56
00:03:23.166 --> 00:03:26.000
See?! It gave us a perfect translation!

57
00:03:26.066 --> 00:03:28.066
Science is so amazing!

58
00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.833
Pan? Cham!

59
00:03:29.899 --> 00:03:31.333
Pika!

60
00:03:31.399 --> 00:03:33.399
Did they really say that stuff?

61
00:03:33.466 --> 00:03:35.466
Who knows? Maybe they did.

62
00:03:35.533 --> 00:03:38.100
I’ll guess they’re probably saying what Ash said,

63
00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:40.333
that Chespin should share its food with them.

64
00:03:40.399 --> 00:03:43.333
Pan Cham!

65
00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:46.266
Why didn’t my machine function properly?

66
00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:50.433
I suppose my invention could have chosen its words poorly.

67
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.600
- Pik! Pika! Pikapi!
- What, Pikachu?

68
00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:57.500
-I bet you're hungry.

69
00:03:57.566 --> 00:03:59.566
- I’ll get you some food!
- Pika?

70
00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:02.833
You know, perhaps Ash was correct after all.

71
00:04:02.899 --> 00:04:05.633
Whoa!

72
00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.133
Okay! Here you are!

73
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.566
Pan Cham!

74
00:04:10.633 --> 00:04:15.700
Pan Cham, Cham! Cham, Cham! Cham! Pan Cham, Cham, Cham, Cham!

75
00:04:15.766 --> 00:04:18.300
- Pan Cham, Cham, Cham, Cham!
- Fen?

76
00:04:18.366 --> 00:04:20.733
- Pan Cham, Cham, Cham!
- Huh?

77
00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:23.366
Pan!

78
00:04:23.433 --> 00:04:26.266
- They ate everything we had!
- Ches, Ches, Ches, Ches!

79
00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:28.766
My Pokémon Translator was right!

80
00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:31.866
It said they said that what we have belongs to everyone,

81
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:34.433
which means our lunch belongs to the Pancham, too!

82
00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.766
- It said what?
- And that doesn’t help us at all now!

83
00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:40.800
Like I said, science is so amazing!

84
00:04:40.866 --> 00:04:43.166
Aw, I guess you could say that!

85
00:04:43.233 --> 00:04:45.400
Pika Pikachu!

86
00:04:45.466 --> 00:04:47.900
- Aim!
- Fire!

87
00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:50.500
Pikachu!

88
00:04:50.566 --> 00:04:52.333
- Pikachu!
- Froakie!

89
00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.400
- Fennekin!
- Chespin!

90
00:04:53.466 --> 00:04:55.400
Pan Cham!

91
00:04:55.466 --> 00:04:59.166
-Pikachu’s ours. Friends included!

92
00:04:59.233 --> 00:05:01.866
- Team Rocket!
- Surprise, surprise!

93
00:05:01.933 --> 00:05:04.500
- Time flies!
- Away to the skies!

94
00:05:04.566 --> 00:05:06.666
- Stop!
- Oh, no they don’t!

95
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:11.866
- After them, Fletchling!
- Fletch, Fletchling!

96
00:05:11.933 --> 00:05:13.800
Not so fast!

97
00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.500
- Inkay, ink!
- Inkay, go!

98
00:05:17.566 --> 00:05:21.833
-Fletch, Fletch, Fletchling! Fletch!

99
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.333
Fletchling, oh no!

100
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.833
- No? Oh, yes!
- Wobbuffet!

101
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.733
- Come on. Let’s go!
- Right behind you!

102
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.200
- Please, help Chespin!
- You can count on me, Bonnie!

103
00:05:35.266 --> 00:05:38.566
Yay! A job well done!

104
00:05:38.633 --> 00:05:41.066
There’s nothing like work that’s lots of fun!

105
00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.766
In the Boss’s eyes, we’ll be second to none!

106
00:05:43.833 --> 00:05:45.300
Wobbuffet!

107
00:05:45.366 --> 00:05:48.666
Hey! We’re taking you to Team Rocket headquarters

108
00:05:48.733 --> 00:05:53.433
and turn you into a bunch of useful members of Team Rocket society!

109
00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.800
James, shall we notify headquarters?

110
00:05:55.866 --> 00:05:57.866
- Hold the phone!
- Huh?

111
00:05:57.933 --> 00:06:01.266
Who’s going to get the credit for this ingenious job?

112
00:06:02.566 --> 00:06:05.000
Well, I invented the capture machine.

113
00:06:05.066 --> 00:06:07.500
Yeah? Well, I came up with the plan.

114
00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:12.000
Well, I’m the one who pointed out the key point. It’s a no-brainer!

115
00:06:12.066 --> 00:06:14.933
You don’t get credit for a stupid thing like that!

116
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.099
- Oh, yeah? Timing is everything!
- Look, dopes, without a plan in place,

117
00:06:19.166 --> 00:06:21.733
everything else is nothing but a plate with no grub on it!

118
00:06:21.799 --> 00:06:24.799
Remember, it was my Inkay who stopped those Twerps

119
00:06:24.866 --> 00:06:27.166
in their tracks from chasing after us, right?

120
00:06:27.233 --> 00:06:32.233
And lest you forget who Inkay’s Trainer is. Face it! I deserve the credit in full!

121
00:06:32.299 --> 00:06:36.500
Stop! Enough! I say we decide this mess with a battle!

122
00:06:36.566 --> 00:06:39.333
- I’ll fight the good fight!
- You’re on, chumps!

123
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.766
Inkay, use Psybeam!

124
00:06:41.833 --> 00:06:44.500
- Wobbuffet, you’re up!
- Wob, Buff, Buff!

125
00:06:49.266 --> 00:06:51.266
-Pika!

126
00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:53.233
- You overdid it!
- Whoa!

127
00:06:53.299 --> 00:06:58.366
- Uh! Team Rocket’s balloon exploded!
- Our poor Pokémon.

128
00:06:58.433 --> 00:07:02.299
- So, we need Dedenne’s help!
- Dedenne’s help?

129
00:07:02.366 --> 00:07:03.966
When we first met Dedenne,

130
00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:07.033
it was utilizing electrical energy to communicate!

131
00:07:09.566 --> 00:07:10.766
Yeah, that's right!

132
00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:14.599
Dedenne, it’d be great if you could pick up on Pikachu’s electricity!

133
00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:17.366
- Na, na!
- Wow, Dedenne can really do that?

134
00:07:17.433 --> 00:07:21.033
- That’s incredible!
- Just wait and see!

135
00:07:21.099 --> 00:07:25.599
Dedenne, the first thing you need to do is figure out where Pikachu’s energy is.

136
00:07:25.666 --> 00:07:28.166
- We’re counting on you, Dedenne!
- Na, Na!

137
00:07:40.799 --> 00:07:43.733
Sorry about that, bub. I had a lousy flight plan.

138
00:07:43.799 --> 00:07:48.433
-Argh! I said I was sorry!

139
00:07:52.533 --> 00:07:54.700
Froakie!

140
00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.700
Froak, Froak!

141
00:07:59.933 --> 00:08:01.266
Fro!

142
00:08:01.333 --> 00:08:06.566
- Brr! Pika, Pika!
- Kie? Fro!

143
00:08:06.633 --> 00:08:08.500
Pika, Pika!

144
00:08:08.566 --> 00:08:10.000
Froakie!

145
00:08:10.066 --> 00:08:13.866
Pik, Pik! Pik, Ka!

146
00:08:13.933 --> 00:08:15.433
Froak!

147
00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.266
Pika, Pika!

148
00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:21.866
Fro, Fro!

149
00:08:21.933 --> 00:08:24.966
- Ches, Ches, Ches, Ches!
- Pika!

150
00:08:25.033 --> 00:08:27.333
- Pikachu!
- Kie!

151
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.533
-Pika!

152
00:08:30.599 --> 00:08:34.433
Pin! Ches!

153
00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.500
- Pin!
- Pika!

154
00:08:36.566 --> 00:08:38.566
Pikachu!

155
00:08:41.799 --> 00:08:45.533
- Pika Pikachu!
- Pikachu, be a pal and help me down!

156
00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:49.400
- Pika!
- We’re both Pokémon, right?

157
00:08:49.466 --> 00:08:50.699
- Fro!
- Pika?

158
00:08:50.766 --> 00:08:53.800
- Froakie!
- Chespin! Ches, Ches!

159
00:08:56.699 --> 00:09:00.733
- Pika.
- Yeah! Sounds like okay to me!

160
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.100
- Pika, Pika!
- Fen!

161
00:09:03.166 --> 00:09:05.266
Chespin!

162
00:09:08.166 --> 00:09:09.800
Froakie!

163
00:09:09.866 --> 00:09:13.766
Thanks, all you lugs. What do you say we call a truce, pal?

164
00:09:13.833 --> 00:09:16.833
- Pikachu!
- I knew I could count on you, buddy boy!

165
00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:20.566
'Cause that’s just the way you roll!

166
00:09:20.633 --> 00:09:23.500
- Pika, Pika?
- Hey, what was that for?

167
00:09:23.566 --> 00:09:25.400
I was paying you a compliment!

168
00:09:25.466 --> 00:09:26.900
Pikachu!

169
00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:30.100
Well, just as long as you understand.

170
00:09:30.166 --> 00:09:34.199
If I see that log again, I’ll use these dopes as a shield!

171
00:09:34.266 --> 00:09:36.633
Huh?

172
00:09:36.699 --> 00:09:39.166
- Fro, Froakie!
- Pika, Pika!

173
00:09:39.233 --> 00:09:41.400
- Chespin!
- Froakie?

174
00:09:41.466 --> 00:09:42.633
Pikachu!

175
00:09:42.699 --> 00:09:46.433
Pikachu, I’m so glad you and Chespin choose to trust me!

176
00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.033
Chespin’s a chump supremo.

177
00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:52.666
I could use that to my advantage. Talk about a sweet deal!

178
00:09:52.733 --> 00:09:55.333
- Fro!
- Huh?

179
00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:59.933
But this Froakie is a different story.

180
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.699
Who’s that Pokémon?

181
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.033
It’s Pancham!

182
00:10:15.233 --> 00:10:19.633
One teensy little explosion and Meowth goes flying off the handle.

183
00:10:19.699 --> 00:10:21.666
Huh?

184
00:10:21.733 --> 00:10:23.433
Pan Cham, Cham!

185
00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.199
- Look, it’s them!
- The eating machines!

186
00:10:26.266 --> 00:10:27.433
Wobbuff!

187
00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.833
Meeting them here and now must be fate!

188
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.366
Should we grab them and make them ours?

189
00:10:32.433 --> 00:10:35.199
- Wonderful idea!
- Inkay, Psybeam, let’s go!

190
00:10:35.266 --> 00:10:39.033
- Bam!
- Cham!

191
00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:42.100
- Ha-ha!
- How easy can it get?

192
00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:46.933
Huh?

193
00:10:48.466 --> 00:10:50.000
Well, who might you be?

194
00:10:50.066 --> 00:10:52.733
It bears a strange resemblance to those two.

195
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.800
Wobbuffet!

196
00:10:55.966 --> 00:10:59.133
-You’re going to start an ink stink!

197
00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:04.133
That hurts!

198
00:11:04.199 --> 00:11:07.033
Wobbuffet!

199
00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:09.600
Pan Cham, Cham, Cham! Cham, Cham!

200
00:11:12.699 --> 00:11:16.533
Kin! Fenn! Fenn, Fenn!

201
00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.100
- Pika!
- Fen?

202
00:11:21.166 --> 00:11:25.100
Huh? Fenn! Fennekin?

203
00:11:26.066 --> 00:11:28.433
- Pika Pikachu!
- Fennekin!

204
00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.066
Dig! From now on, we’re best of friends!

205
00:11:31.133 --> 00:11:34.833
- Ches, Pin, Pin, Ches, Ches!
- Fennekin!

206
00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:35.933
- Fennekin!
- Pika?

207
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.866
Your fluffy little tail got all dirty, so you want to clean it?

208
00:11:39.933 --> 00:11:40.966
Fennekin!

209
00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.900
You really like to look good, now, don’t you?

210
00:11:43.966 --> 00:11:49.033
- Froakie! Fro!
- Huh? Kin?

211
00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.633
- Fro!
- Fenn!

212
00:11:51.699 --> 00:11:53.466
- Fennekin!
- Pika! Pika!

213
00:11:53.533 --> 00:11:55.033
- Chespin!
- Hey!

214
00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:58.500
So you can use your Frubbles for keeping things all neat-like and tidy!

215
00:11:58.566 --> 00:12:01.666
Fennekin!

216
00:12:01.733 --> 00:12:04.400
Oh, my neck!

217
00:12:04.466 --> 00:12:06.900
This is all your fault, buster.

218
00:12:06.966 --> 00:12:09.666
- What?!
- It was your Inkay...

219
00:12:11.433 --> 00:12:14.199
- Oh, my!
- Ouch!

220
00:12:17.733 --> 00:12:19.533
Pumpkaboo!

221
00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.400
- And who are you?
- Pumpkaboo! Pumpkaboo!

222
00:12:23.466 --> 00:12:25.900
Hm!

223
00:12:25.966 --> 00:12:28.133
- It’s a Pumpkaboo!
- Kaboo, Boo, Boo!

224
00:12:28.199 --> 00:12:29.566
Wobbuffet!

225
00:12:29.633 --> 00:12:31.633
Kab, Kab, Kab, Pump, Pump, Kaboo!

226
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.433
- I caught it!
- No way!!

227
00:12:43.566 --> 00:12:46.766
- Look at Dedenne! Huh?
- Did you find Pikachu!?

228
00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:50.300
Na! Na! Na, Na! Na, Na!

229
00:12:50.366 --> 00:12:51.966
Huh?

230
00:12:52.033 --> 00:12:56.633
- Fen! Fen! Fen!
- Pika?

231
00:12:56.699 --> 00:12:59.866
- It’s a twig! That really tastes good?
- Fen!

232
00:13:01.233 --> 00:13:03.699
Ches! Hm! Ches, Ches, Ches!

233
00:13:03.766 --> 00:13:06.766
Pin, Pin! Ches, Ches! Ches!

234
00:13:08.433 --> 00:13:10.866
Pancham!

235
00:13:10.933 --> 00:13:15.300
- Cranky pants! Whoa!

236
00:13:15.366 --> 00:13:18.633
-Ches, Ches, Ches, Ches!

237
00:13:18.699 --> 00:13:21.699
-Pan, Cham, Cham!

238
00:13:21.766 --> 00:13:24.199
It looks like they’re pals!

239
00:13:30.966 --> 00:13:33.266
Doh...

240
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.233
Pan, Cham, Cham! Pam!

241
00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:37.699
- Ches?
- Huh?

242
00:13:37.766 --> 00:13:39.500
Pan, Cham! Cham, Pan!

243
00:13:39.566 --> 00:13:41.199
- Pikachu!
- Huh?

244
00:13:42.733 --> 00:13:44.666
- Pikapi!
- It’s the Twerp!

245
00:13:44.733 --> 00:13:47.866
- Pika!
- Pikachu, you’re okay!

246
00:13:47.933 --> 00:13:50.166
- Froakie, you okay too?
- Froak!

247
00:13:50.233 --> 00:13:52.433
- Sorry we took so long!
- Yay!

248
00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.666
- Chespin! You okay?
- Ches!

249
00:13:54.733 --> 00:13:57.099
Wow! Isn’t this grand?

250
00:13:57.166 --> 00:13:59.933
Meowth! What are you doing here?!

251
00:14:00.066 --> 00:14:01.733
The Pancham, too!

252
00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.400
Now, don’t all bent out of shape! The problem’s this galoot!

253
00:14:05.466 --> 00:14:07.699
Hm.

254
00:14:07.766 --> 00:14:10.233
Pangoro the Daunting Pokémon,

255
00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.266
and the evolved form of Pancham.

256
00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:16.433
Pangoro has an ornery personality. It holds a bamboo sprig in its mouth,

257
00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.699
which allows Pangoro to detect surrounding movements.

258
00:14:19.766 --> 00:14:21.566
Hey, it looks different again.

259
00:14:21.633 --> 00:14:26.566
I think it’s Chespin’s fault. You see, Chespin broke Pangoro’s bamboo sprig.

260
00:14:26.633 --> 00:14:28.933
So that’s why it looks so down!

261
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.466
Chespin got spooked

262
00:14:30.533 --> 00:14:33.066
and accidentally hit Pangoro with a Pin Missile.

263
00:14:33.133 --> 00:14:37.333
I’m so very sorry. I feel just awful about this!

264
00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.533
- Ches!
- Pan, Cham, Cham, Pan! Cham, Cham, Pan!

265
00:14:40.599 --> 00:14:43.066
These pouty Pancham are fit to be tied!

266
00:14:43.133 --> 00:14:46.500
They’re saying they need to get their paws on another bamboo sprig

267
00:14:46.566 --> 00:14:48.733
so that their leader can get back up to speed.

268
00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.733
But aren’t there lots of bamboo sprigs all around us?

269
00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.300
- Pan, Cham, Cham!
- Pan, Cham!

270
00:14:53.366 --> 00:14:55.533
They’re saying it has to be special bamboo

271
00:14:55.599 --> 00:14:58.233
that only grows on this certain rock a bit up ahead!

272
00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:02.300
It is true that different Pangoro have their own favorite bamboo

273
00:15:02.366 --> 00:15:06.166
and it’s also true that they’ll keep searching for that kind of bamboo

274
00:15:06.233 --> 00:15:07.566
until they find it.

275
00:15:07.633 --> 00:15:08.800
Cham, Cham!

276
00:15:08.866 --> 00:15:10.699
I’ll go and find some.

277
00:15:10.766 --> 00:15:14.466
Since I’m Chespin’s Trainer, it's my responsibility.

278
00:15:14.533 --> 00:15:16.800
Come on, Chespin. Let’s look together!

279
00:15:16.866 --> 00:15:19.233
- I’ll come too!
- We've got to help them!

280
00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:21.300
The sooner the better. Let’s go!

281
00:15:21.366 --> 00:15:24.500
- Pancham, will you show us the way?
- Pan, Cham!

282
00:15:24.566 --> 00:15:26.666
Cham, Cham!

283
00:15:26.733 --> 00:15:30.300
I’ll keep it covered right here! I’m worried about Pangoro!

284
00:15:30.366 --> 00:15:32.800
- What? You worried?
- Fennekin!

285
00:15:32.866 --> 00:15:34.599
I’ve got a heart!

286
00:15:34.666 --> 00:15:37.133
Pan, Cham, Pan!

287
00:15:39.433 --> 00:15:42.433
I’m sorry! It’s my fault you’re dealing with this!

288
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.000
Come on! We’re just helping each other out, like we always do!

289
00:15:46.066 --> 00:15:47.866
Pikachu!

290
00:15:47.933 --> 00:15:50.366
Something worries me about Meowth.

291
00:15:50.433 --> 00:15:53.333
How much trouble can Meowth get into on its own?

292
00:15:54.333 --> 00:15:56.266
- Hey, Meowth?
- Huh?

293
00:15:56.333 --> 00:15:59.533
- Finally! We found you!
- You certainly get around.

294
00:15:59.599 --> 00:16:01.833
- Wo--
- Turn it way down!!

295
00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.833
Palleys! My buds!

296
00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.066
Huh? Huh?

297
00:16:06.133 --> 00:16:08.433
So glad to see your mugs!

298
00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.566
So, what happened to Mr. Big?

299
00:16:10.633 --> 00:16:14.733
That lump turned my good day into a rotten one.

300
00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.300
Here’s the scoop.

301
00:16:18.099 --> 00:16:19.966
Cham, Cham!

302
00:16:20.033 --> 00:16:22.800
- Oh! All the way up there?!
- Pika, Pika!

303
00:16:22.866 --> 00:16:26.966
Why would Pangoro choose to get its bamboo sprig from way up there?

304
00:16:27.033 --> 00:16:29.099
Must be quite the finicky type.

305
00:16:29.166 --> 00:16:31.633
- So, how do we get it?
- I’ll go!

306
00:16:31.699 --> 00:16:36.766
Wait! It’s too dangerous! Don’t worry. I’ll be fine!

307
00:16:36.833 --> 00:16:39.300
- Oh!
- That’s not going to work.

308
00:16:39.366 --> 00:16:41.133
- Pikapi!
- I have an idea!

309
00:16:41.199 --> 00:16:44.333
And it’s a much easier way to get at that bamboo.

310
00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.199
- Huh?
- Use Vine Whip!

311
00:16:47.266 --> 00:16:50.400
- Of course! Let’s try it, Chespin!
- Ches!

312
00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:54.599
- All right, Vine Whip, go!
- Chespin!

313
00:16:58.066 --> 00:17:00.233
Pin!

314
00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:02.533
Yay!!

315
00:17:02.599 --> 00:17:04.599
- Pan, Pan!
- Pan, Cham!

316
00:17:05.599 --> 00:17:08.466
- Pangoro! We got it!
- Pan, Cham, Cham!

317
00:17:08.533 --> 00:17:11.000
Huh? Team Rocket!

318
00:17:11.066 --> 00:17:13.233
Meowth! I knew it!

319
00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:16.300
You dumb Twerps!

320
00:17:16.366 --> 00:17:19.300
It’s a family reunion with the Team Rocket clan!

321
00:17:19.366 --> 00:17:21.733
We thought we’d wait and wish you welcome.

322
00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.566
You’d better let Pangoro and Pancham go now!

323
00:17:24.633 --> 00:17:26.933
- You tell 'em!
- Oh? Got battle fever?

324
00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:30.600
Okay, Pikachu. Come with us if you know what’s good for you.

325
00:17:30.666 --> 00:17:33.066
It’d be a drag to see them used as scratching posts!

326
00:17:33.133 --> 00:17:34.866
- As what?
- Pikachu!

327
00:17:34.933 --> 00:17:37.266
You cowards! Pangoro can’t even move!

328
00:17:37.333 --> 00:17:38.766
Aren’t we smart!

329
00:17:38.833 --> 00:17:41.700
Say, take a look at my catch of the day!

330
00:17:41.766 --> 00:17:44.566
Now, Team Rocket is stronger than ever!

331
00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:48.399
- Pumpkaboo!
- Cool! When’d you get that?

332
00:17:48.466 --> 00:17:51.300
So Team Rocket’s got a new Pokémon!

333
00:17:53.466 --> 00:17:55.933
Pumpkaboo, the Pumpkin Pokémon.

334
00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:59.000
Pumpkaboo’s eyes can glow, which lights the way for travelers.

335
00:17:59.066 --> 00:18:00.833
They often sleep in the ground.

336
00:18:00.899 --> 00:18:02.899
All right, Pumpkaboo, Leech Seed!

337
00:18:02.966 --> 00:18:05.466
Kaboo!

338
00:18:09.466 --> 00:18:13.399
Oh!

339
00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:18.133
Pikachu!

340
00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:22.733
See? Leech Seed has the unbelievable power to siphon off your power!

341
00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.733
Now, really put the squeeze on them!

342
00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:27.600
- Ash, what are we going to do?!
- Uh...

343
00:18:27.666 --> 00:18:30.000
Maybe if we can get the bamboo sprig

344
00:18:30.066 --> 00:18:33.000
we brought into Pangoro’s mouth, it’ll be able to help!

345
00:18:33.066 --> 00:18:36.633
- Okay!
- Pika, Pika!

346
00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:40.266
Look at this, Pangoro! We got the bamboo you like!

347
00:18:42.333 --> 00:18:45.833
- What is that Twerp doing?
- Okay, Inkay, Psybeam!

348
00:18:45.899 --> 00:18:48.566
Pika! Pikachu!

349
00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:53.266
Pikachu!

350
00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:59.433
Pumpkaboo, use Shadow Ball!

351
00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.666
Kab, Kab, Kab, Kab, Boo!

352
00:19:07.733 --> 00:19:09.533
- What?
- Argh!

353
00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.399
- Fenn!
- Ches!

354
00:19:13.466 --> 00:19:16.466
- Wobbuffet, go!
- Wobbuff!

355
00:19:16.533 --> 00:19:18.333
Wobbuff!

356
00:19:21.633 --> 00:19:23.466
Here goes...

357
00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:30.766
Got it?

358
00:19:35.833 --> 00:19:36.833
All right!

359
00:19:40.866 --> 00:19:43.966
- We’re blasting off!

360
00:19:44.033 --> 00:19:46.666
- Pump!
- Again!

361
00:19:51.133 --> 00:19:53.433
- You’re all right!
- Way to go, Ash!

362
00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.666
-Pikachu!

363
00:19:55.733 --> 00:20:00.433
- Pangoro’s so strong!
- The power of that bamboo is awesome!

364
00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.866
Thanks a lot for getting us out of a tough jam, Pangoro!

365
00:20:03.933 --> 00:20:07.300
We know we caused a lot of trouble for you. We’re sorry.

366
00:20:07.366 --> 00:20:08.866
Pin!

367
00:20:08.933 --> 00:20:10.733
Pangoro!

368
00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:13.566
Pan, Cham! Cham, Cham!

369
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.899
- See you later!
- Pika!

370
00:20:23.966 --> 00:20:27.666
And so, with their unexpected detour behind them,

371
00:20:27.733 --> 00:20:29.866
our heroes leave the bamboo forest,

372
00:20:29.933 --> 00:20:33.733
but it seems they’ve forgotten something important...

373
00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:36.866
Whoa! We never finished lunch!

374
00:20:36.933 --> 00:20:39.800
- We totally forgot about eating!
- Pika!

375
00:20:39.866 --> 00:20:43.100
Now that you mention it, my tummy feels a bit rumbly.

376
00:20:43.166 --> 00:20:45.766
- Oh!

377
00:20:45.833 --> 00:20:50.899
..as the journey continues!
